{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792858832712,"sessionID":"ses_e914a8a92ffed6Ny0syywiP6Oa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_qorKxXOPHJFS3GQr9giC7375","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-24\\20-brief.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-24\\20-brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brief — 2026-10-24\n2: \n3: ## The use case\n4: \n5: Orienteers post their split times after every race on Attackpoint and club/WinSplits\n6: result pages, and everyone asks the same question: \"where did I lose time?\" WinSplits\n7: already computes the answer — a per-leg \"time loss\" with mistake legs coloured pink —\n8: but it lives in a results-table web page nobody can post. This template turns one\n9: racer's IOF XML 3.0 result row into a shareable, deterministic split-analysis card.\n10: \n11: ## The template\n12: \n13: - id: `@one-a-day/sports/orienteering-split-analysis/v1`\n14: - pack: `sports` (existing — an orienteering split card is a race-recap card exactly\n15:   like the swimming, HYROX, erg and golf cards already in this pack; no new pack).\n16: - title: `Orienteering Split Analysis` (scaffold renders `2026-10-24 · Orienteering Split Analysis`)\n17: - kind: **still image**; canvas hint **1280x720** (landscape, the shape of a WinSplits\n18:   table read left-to-right). Must also work at portrait 1080x1920 and square 1080x1080,\n19:   and the seven-contract-canvas sweep at defaults.\n20: - duration: still.\n21: \n22: ## Layout\n23: \n24: A card in three vertical bands: header, a control-by-control body, footer.\n25: \n26: ```\n27: +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n28: | EMMA LINDQVIST                        FINISH  45:02          |\n29: | OK Klyftamo · W21E                   PLACE   #12   +1:23     |\n30: | Middle, 4.2 km                                             |\n31: +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n32: | ctrl |         split tape (slowest leg = full)    | split | loss |\n33: |  1   | [#################]                       | 4:08  | +0:47 |  <-- pink\n34: |  2   | [##########]                              | 2:41  | 0:00  |\n35: |  ...                                                        |\n36: |  F   | [########]                                | 1:55  | 0:00  |\n37: +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n38: | TIME W/O MISTAKES  42:04        TOTAL LOSS  +2:58   BEST LEG  1:32 |\n39: +--------------------------------------------------------------+\n40: ```\n41: \n42: - **Header (top ~0–0.26 of H).** Left: name (bold), then `club · class`, then `course`\n43:   (dim). Right: the finish time as the hero figure with a `FINISH` label, a place chip\n44:   (`#12`, accent fill), and `+1:23` as the time-behind line. The finish is the number a\n45:   screenshot buries, so it is the largest text on the card.\n46: - **Body (~0.26–0.80 of H).** One row per leg, in course order. Columns: control code\n47:   (dim, right-aligned), the split tape, split time (bold, right), time loss (right).\n48:   The tape bar's length is `split / slowestSplit` — the slowest leg fills the track,\n49:   every other leg is shorter in proportion. A leg with `loss > 0` is a **mistake leg**:\n50:   its bar is filled in the accent (pink), its loss text is accent-coloured and signed\n51:   (`+0:47`); a clean leg gets a neutral bar and `0:00` (or an empty loss cell).\n52: - **Footer (bottom ~0.80–1.0 of H).** Three cells: `TIME W/O MISTAKES`, `TOTAL LOSS`,\n53:   `BEST LEG`. Time-without-mistakes = finish − total loss; total loss = Σ leg loss;\n54:   best leg = min split. All three are arithmetic on the entered numbers, so the card\n55:   can verify them — no class-relative claim is re-derived.\n56: \n57: ## Layout contract (the invariants the build sweeps)\n58: \n59: - **Every text fits its box** — `tag` every text source and give each label a\n60:   `textFitsMeasured` (the header block is fitted against the real font, so measured is\n61:   exact).\n62: - **Bands** — `name`/`club`/`class`/`course`/`finish`/`place`/`behind` and the place\n63:   chip `within { yFrac: [0, 0.26] }`; every body row and its cells `within\n64:   { yFrac: [0.26, 0.80] }`; the three footer cells and their values `within\n65:   { yFrac: [0.80, 1] }`.\n66: - **Presence + shape** — the place chip is `{ label }` present; the tape column is\n67:   `minWidthFrac: 0.32` so the bars read as bars at every aspect; the full-width row\n68:   bands are present for every leg.\n69: - **Relation** — all body rows `equal: \"size\"` (tolerance 2px), and the three footer\n70:   cells equal size.\n71: - No exact fractions are pinned beyond the three bands and the tape width — the use\n72:   case does not ask for pixel positions.\n73: \n74: ## Props (name · type · default · what it changes · required?)\n75: \n76: 1. `name` · string · `\"Emma Lindqvist\"` · header bold line · no (empty hides)\n77: 2. `club` · string · `\"OK Klyftamo\"` · header second line · no (empty hides)\n78: 3. `className` · string · `\"W21E\"` · class, joined after club · no\n79: 4. `course` · string · `\"Middle, 4.2 km\"` · header third line · no (empty hides)\n80: 5. `finish` · string · `\"45:02\"` · the hero figure, `m:ss` / `h:mm:ss` · no (fail-fast if unparseable)\n81: 6. `place` · number · `12` · the place chip `#12`; 0 hides the chip · no\n82: 7. `behind` · string · `\"+1:23\"` · time behind winner, printed as entered · no\n83: 8. `splits` · json list · a 12-control middle course (13 legs incl. the `F` finish\n84:    leg) · the body rows · no. Each item `{ control: string, split: \"m:ss\", loss: \"m:ss\" }`;\n85:    `loss` is the WinSplits per-leg time loss, `0:00` = clean. Min 4 legs, max 18.\n86: 9. `accent` · color · `#d94f8c` · the mistake-leg pink (bars + loss text + place chip) · no\n87: 10. `preset` · string · `\"dark\"` · page and ink, `\"dark\"` | `\"light\"` · no\n88: 11. `debugLayout` · boolean · `false` · draws the contract over the card (dev-only) · no\n89: \n90: The `splits` json schema (via `meta.constraints.jsonSchema`) mirrors the IOF field\n91: names (`control`, `split`, `loss`) so the editor surfaces a structured form.\n92: \n93: ## Beats\n94: \n95: Still image — no beats.\n96: \n97: ## Defaults must show\n98: \n99: With no inputs the gate renders a legible dark card: the name/club/class/course header,\n100: `45:02` as the hero, a `#12` chip and `+1:23`, a 13-row body in course order with\n101: three mistake legs drawn pink and their loss signed, and a footer reading\n102: `TIME W/O MISTAKES 42:04 · TOTAL LOSS +2:58 · BEST LEG 1:32` (computed from the\n103: entered splits). The \"where did I lose time?\" answer is visible at a glance: pink =\n104: mistake, bar length = split.\n105: \n106: ## Acceptance rubric (the critic scores against this)\n107: \n108: 1. **The question reads instantly.** Bar length = split length; mistake legs (`loss > 0`)\n109:    are pink in both bar and loss text; clean legs are neutral. No legend needed.\n110: 2. **The header is the result.** Finish time is the largest text; name/club/class/course,\n111:    place chip and time-behind are all in the top band and all fit at defaults.\n112: 3. **Honest math.** `loss` per leg is taken as a prop (never re-derived — it is WinSplits'\n113:    class-relative number); total loss and time-without-mistakes are computed from it and\n114:    printed consistently; `finish` is printed as entered and not checked against the split\n115:    sum.\n116: 4. **Layout contract holds at the seven canvases at defaults** — every text fits, header/\n117:    body/footer in their bands, rows equal height, tape ≥ 32% wide — and the template's own\n118:    test sweeps the stress copy (a long club name, a 4-leg course, an 18-leg course, light\n119:    preset, a mistake on the last leg).\n120: 5. **Deterministic and fail-fast.** No clock/random/ambient state; same props → identical\n121:    m0 (the gate diffs twice). A malformed time (decimal, over 99:59:59), a non-`m:ss` loss,\n122:    a control count outside 4–18, or a name longer than the fit floor throws a clear\n123:    `@one-a-day/...: <field> <rule>` error instead of rendering.\n124: \n125: ## Variants worth trying (each ONE idea, not a rewrite)\n126: \n127: - **a (primary):** dark card, bar = split length, pink fills the mistake leg's bar and its\n128:   loss text; clean legs leave the loss cell blank.\n129: - **b (layout):** loss-first — the time-loss column becomes the emphasised, right-of-tape\n130:   figure and the split time dims, so the \"mistake\" column is what the eye lands on; the\n131:   whole mistake row also gets a thin pink left rule + a pink wash.\n132: - **c (motion):** a short video reveal — the tape bars draw on left-to-right in leg order\n133:   (pink legs land pink) and the finish time counts up; same geometry, `ctx.target.durationMs`\n134:   as the clock.\n\n(End of file - total 134 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brief — 2026-10-24\n\n## The use case\n\nOrienteers post their split times after every race on Attackpoint and club/WinSplits\nresult pages, and everyone asks the same question: \"where did I lose time?\" WinSplits\nalready computes the answer — a per-leg \"time loss\" with mistake legs coloured pink —\nbut it lives in a results-table web page nobody can post. This template turns one\nracer's IOF XML 3.0 result row into a shareable, deterministic split-analysis card.\n\n## The template\n\n- id: `@one-a-day/sports/orienteering-split-analysis/v1`\n- pack: `sports` (existing — an orienteering split card is a race-recap card exactly\n  like the swimming, HYROX, erg and golf cards already in this pack; no new pack).\n- title: `Orienteering Split Analysis` (scaffold renders `2026-10-24 · Orienteering Split Analysis`)\n- kind: **still image**; canvas hint **1280x720** (landscape, the shape of a WinSplits\n  table read left-to-right). Must also work at portrait 1080x1920 and square 1080x1080,\n  and the seven-contract-canvas sweep at defaults.\n- duration: still.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-24\\20-brief.md","text":"# Brief — 2026-10-24\n\n## The use case\n\nOrienteers post their split times after every race on Attackpoint and club/WinSplits\nresult pages, and everyone asks the same question: \"where did I lose time?\" WinSplits\nalready computes the answer — a per-leg \"time loss\" with mistake legs coloured pink —\nbut it lives in a results-table web page nobody can post. This template turns one\nracer's IOF XML 3.0 result row into a shareable, deterministic split-analysis card.\n\n## The template\n\n- id: `@one-a-day/sports/orienteering-split-analysis/v1`\n- pack: `sports` (existing — an orienteering split card is a race-recap card exactly\n  like the swimming, HYROX, erg and golf cards already in this pack; no new pack).\n- title: `Orienteering Split Analysis` (scaffold renders `2026-10-24 · Orienteering Split Analysis`)\n- kind: **still image**; canvas hint **1280x720** (landscape, the shape of a WinSplits\n  table read left-to-right). Must also work at portrait 1080x1920 and square 1080x1080,\n  and the seven-contract-canvas sweep at defaults.\n- duration: still.\n\n## Layout\n\nA card in three vertical bands: header, a control-by-control body, footer.\n\n```\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EMMA LINDQVIST                        FINISH  45:02          |\n| OK Klyftamo · W21E                   PLACE   #12   +1:23     |\n| Middle, 4.2 km                                             |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n| ctrl |         split tape (slowest leg = full)    | split | loss |\n|  1   | [#################]                       | 4:08  | +0:47 |  <-- pink\n|  2   | [##########]                              | 2:41  | 0:00  |\n|  ...                                                        |\n|  F   | [########]                                | 1:55  | 0:00  |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n| TIME W/O MISTAKES  42:04        TOTAL LOSS  +2:58   BEST LEG  1:32 |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n- **Header (top ~0–0.26 of H).** Left: name (bold), then `club · class`, then `course`\n  (dim). Right: the finish time as the hero figure with a `FINISH` label, a place chip\n  (`#12`, accent fill), and `+1:23` as the time-behind line. The finish is the number a\n  screenshot buries, so it is the largest text on the card.\n- **Body (~0.26–0.80 of H).** One row per leg, in course order. Columns: control code\n  (dim, right-aligned), the split tape, split time (bold, right), time loss (right).\n  The tape bar's length is `split / slowestSplit` — the slowest leg fills the track,\n  every other leg is shorter in proportion. A leg with `loss > 0` is a **mistake leg**:\n  its bar is filled in the accent (pink), its loss text is accent-coloured and signed\n  (`+0:47`); a clean leg gets a neutral bar and `0:00` (or an empty loss cell).\n- **Footer (bottom ~0.80–1.0 of H).** Three cells: `TIME W/O MISTAKES`, `TOTAL LOSS`,\n  `BEST LEG`. Time-without-mistakes = finish − total loss; total loss = Σ leg loss;\n  best leg = min split. All three are arithmetic on the entered numbers, so the card\n  can verify them — no class-relative claim is re-derived.\n\n## Layout contract (the invariants the build sweeps)\n\n- **Every text fits its box** — `tag` every text source and give each label a\n  `textFitsMeasured` (the header block is fitted against the real font, so measured is\n  exact).\n- **Bands** — `name`/`club`/`class`/`course`/`finish`/`place`/`behind` and the place\n  chip `within { yFrac: [0, 0.26] }`; every body row and its cells `within\n  { yFrac: [0.26, 0.80] }`; the three footer cells and their values `within\n  { yFrac: [0.80, 1] }`.\n- **Presence + shape** — the place chip is `{ label }` present; the tape column is\n  `minWidthFrac: 0.32` so the bars read as bars at every aspect; the full-width row\n  bands are present for every leg.\n- **Relation** — all body rows `equal: \"size\"` (tolerance 2px), and the three footer\n  cells equal size.\n- No exact fractions are pinned beyond the three bands and the tape width — the use\n  case does not ask for pixel positions.\n\n## Props (name · type · default · what it changes · required?)\n\n1. `name` · string · `\"Emma Lindqvist\"` · header bold line · no (empty hides)\n2. `club` · string · `\"OK Klyftamo\"` · header second line · no (empty hides)\n3. `className` · string · `\"W21E\"` · class, joined after club · no\n4. `course` · string · `\"Middle, 4.2 km\"` · header third line · no (empty hides)\n5. `finish` · string · `\"45:02\"` · the hero figure, `m:ss` / `h:mm:ss` · no (fail-fast if unparseable)\n6. `place` · number · `12` · the place chip `#12`; 0 hides the chip · no\n7. `behind` · string · `\"+1:23\"` · time behind winner, printed as entered · no\n8. `splits` · json list · a 12-control middle course (13 legs incl. the `F` finish\n   leg) · the body rows · no. Each item `{ control: string, split: \"m:ss\", loss: \"m:ss\" }`;\n   `loss` is the WinSplits per-leg time loss, `0:00` = clean. Min 4 legs, max 18.\n9. `accent` · color · `#d94f8c` · the mistake-leg pink (bars + loss text + place chip) · no\n10. `preset` · string · `\"dark\"` · page and ink, `\"dark\"` | `\"light\"` · no\n11. `debugLayout` · boolean · `false` · draws the contract over the card (dev-only) · no\n\nThe `splits` json schema (via `meta.constraints.jsonSchema`) mirrors the IOF field\nnames (`control`, `split`, `loss`) so the editor surfaces a structured form.\n\n## Beats\n\nStill image — no beats.\n\n## Defaults must show\n\nWith no inputs the gate renders a legible dark card: the name/club/class/course header,\n`45:02` as the hero, a `#12` chip and `+1:23`, a 13-row body in course order with\nthree mistake legs drawn pink and their loss signed, and a footer reading\n`TIME W/O MISTAKES 42:04 · TOTAL LOSS +2:58 · BEST LEG 1:32` (computed from the\nentered splits). The \"where did I lose time?\" answer is visible at a glance: pink =\nmistake, bar length = split.\n\n## Acceptance rubric (the critic scores against this)\n\n1. **The question reads instantly.** Bar length = split length; mistake legs (`loss > 0`)\n   are pink in both bar and loss text; clean legs are neutral. No legend needed.\n2. **The header is the result.** Finish time is the largest text; name/club/class/course,\n   place chip and time-behind are all in the top band and all fit at defaults.\n3. **Honest math.** `loss` per leg is taken as a prop (never re-derived — it is WinSplits'\n   class-relative number); total loss and time-without-mistakes are computed from it and\n   printed consistently; `finish` is printed as entered and not checked against the split\n   sum.\n4. **Layout contract holds at the seven canvases at defaults** — every text fits, header/\n   body/footer in their bands, rows equal height, tape ≥ 32% wide — and the template's own\n   test sweeps the stress copy (a long club name, a 4-leg course, an 18-leg course, light\n   preset, a mistake on the last leg).\n5. **Deterministic and fail-fast.** No clock/random/ambient state; same props → identical\n   m0 (the gate diffs twice). A malformed time (decimal, over 99:59:59), a non-`m:ss` loss,\n   a control count outside 4–18, or a name longer than the fit floor throws a clear\n   `@one-a-day/...: <field> <rule>` error instead of rendering.\n\n## Variants worth trying (each ONE idea, not a rewrite)\n\n- **a (primary):** dark card, bar = split length, pink fills the mistake leg's bar and its\n  loss text; clean legs leave the loss cell blank.\n- **b (layout):** loss-first — the time-loss column becomes the emphasised, right-of-tape\n  figure and the split time dims, so the \"mistake\" column is what the eye lands on; the\n  whole mistake row also gets a thin pink left rule + a pink wash.\n- **c (motion):** a short video reveal — the tape bars draw on left-to-right in leg order\n  (pink legs land pink) and the finish time counts up; same geometry, `ctx.target.durationMs`\n  as the clock.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":134,"totalLines":134,"truncated":false}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-24\\20-brief.md","time":{"start":1792858832696,"end":1792858832710}},"id":"prt_16eb6be3f001MR1hXuBt7t34kY","sessionID":"ses_e914a8a92ffed6Ny0syywiP6Oa","messageID":"msg_16eb5777e001LOM2ZMSl5DHkbN"}}
